WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.655
Coming up soon, we'll be adding multiple cats,

00:00:02.655 --> 00:00:06.555
so we're going to get ready by moving the model to a separate area.

00:00:06.555 --> 00:00:09.810
Because if we left the model where it is in the view model,

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:14.560
we'd be putting all of this into a for loop and making it again,

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.025
and again, and again.

00:00:16.025 --> 00:00:19.785
There's gotta be a more separated and readable way to do this.

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:22.770
All of this code that I'm selecting here should

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:26.640
move into a special function which will make us new cats.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.295
I'm going to cut all of it, and wow!

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.200
Look at how simple our view model is.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.700
We'll call this function Cat with a capital C. As you can see,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.180
all of the Cat logic is here inside of

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.675
our cat function and our view model down here, is super simple.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.860
Now we do still need to actually make this cat.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.225
I'm going to store our cat in a current cat variable,

00:00:49.225 --> 00:00:51.925
specifically, a knockout observable.

00:00:51.925 --> 00:00:55.280
And instead of passing in an object literal like this,

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.560
I'm going to pass in a new cat.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.590
And that should work. Well, almost.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:03.665
We actually just changed where our cat lives.

00:01:03.665 --> 00:01:07.460
Now instead of finding our cats properties right on the view model,

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.595
we need to look inside of the current cat variable.

00:01:10.595 --> 00:01:12.730
So, over in our HTML,

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.435
we need to make a couple changes.

00:01:14.435 --> 00:01:16.110
So here in our HTML,

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.235
we need to change all the data bind properties

00:01:18.235 --> 00:01:21.175
that are looking for Cat-related properties.

00:01:21.175 --> 00:01:27.310
They all need to be currentCat.name, currentCat.title, etcetera.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.200
That's because, once again,

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.410
our Cat is not living on the view model anymore,

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.860
our cat is living in the current Cat observable.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.830
And remember, we put the parentheses here because

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:43.905
current Cat is actually a knockout observable which is a function.

00:01:43.905 --> 00:01:46.535
In order to get the current Cat value,

00:01:46.535 --> 00:01:49.945
we need to run that function and it'll return the value to us.

00:01:49.945 --> 00:01:53.335
Lets hop over to our browser and hit refresh.

00:01:53.335 --> 00:01:56.540
Sure enough, everything seems to work just fine.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:57.870
We have our nicknames,

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:00.415
our cat image and all of this.

00:02:00.415 --> 00:02:02.065
If we try to click, however,

00:02:02.065 --> 00:02:07.430
we get an uncaught type error: undefined is not a function, line 34.

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:09.735
In our code, app.js,

00:02:09.735 --> 00:02:13.695
for me, line 34 is this right here.

00:02:13.695 --> 00:02:15.850
Now what's the problem with this?

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.575
What is this.clickCount?

00:02:18.575 --> 00:02:24.430
Well, "this" represents the view model and there is no click count on the viewmodel.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:28.940
Remember, clickcount is now living inside of our current cat.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:33.610
In this case, I need to say this.currentCat().clickcount

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:38.410
is going to be this.currentCat.clickcount()+1.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:41.300
And now if I go back into the browser and I hit refresh,

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.435
sure enough, my clicking works just fine.

00:02:44.435 --> 00:02:46.585
Go ahead and make those main changes.

00:02:46.585 --> 00:02:50.675
First of all, moving your cat into a separate cat function.

00:02:50.675 --> 00:02:54.605
Secondly, updating the bindings and your index.html file.

00:02:54.605 --> 00:02:57.500
And finally, updating our increment counter,

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:01.155
so that way, it can get the click count properly from the model.

00:03:01.155 --> 00:03:03.610
Go ahead and make those changes.

